---
source: crates/aido-wire/tests/contract_snapshots.rs
expression: table
---
 1  request_too_large
    the request is longer than the broker reads; no rule permits a command this long, so shorten it rather than retrying
 2  request_timed_out
    the request did not arrive complete before the broker's timeout; aido sends it in one write, so retry the aido command
 3  request_unreadable
    the connection failed while the request was being read; retry the aido command
 4  request_not_utf8
    the request is not UTF-8; aido refuses a non-UTF-8 argument before it sends anything, so this request did not come from aido
 5  request_malformed
    the request is not a broker request; install aido and aidod from the same release
 6  request_wrong_schema
    the request declares a schema this broker does not implement; install aido and aidod from the same release
 7  program_not_absolute
    name the program by its absolute path; the broker never searches PATH
 8  interior_nul
    an argument contains a NUL byte, which the kernel would cut short; remove it
 9  peer_unidentified
    the broker could not establish which process asked; retry, and if it persists run `aido doctor` to see whether this host can identify a caller
10  spool_unusable
    the broker cannot use its spool; an administrator must check that /run/aido/req is a root-owned 0700 directory (systemd-tmpfiles --create)
11  spool_full
    too many requests are pending; wait for them to be used or to expire, then retry the aido command
12  policy_unloadable
    the root-owned ruleset or settings could not be loaded and the broker is failing closed; an administrator must run `aido check` and `aido doctor`
13  nonce_collision
    the broker drew a nonce that already names a request, so its random source is broken; an administrator must investigate before anything is retried
14  broker_unusable
    the broker could not complete the request and failed closed; an administrator should read the broker's audit record in the journal
15  broker_audit_unavailable
    the broker could not write the audit record, so it minted nothing and failed closed; an administrator must check that /var/lib/aido is a root-owned 0700 directory with room to write and that journald is running
